# LEXOS Coding Agent Workflow

Every coding task must map to a work packet in:

`docs/implementation/05 Work Packet Register.md`

Use a branch named:

`dev/<tool>-<task>`

Examples:

- `dev/cursor-foundation`
- `dev/cursor-schema`
- `dev/codex-w4-extraction`
- `dev/codex-support-matrix`

Before starting, confirm:

- active branch;
- active work packet;
- allowed files/folders;
- prohibited files/folders;
- required source documents;
- acceptance criteria;
- tests required.

Do not edit outside the allowed scope.

Stop and report if the task requires touching prohibited files.

Update `AGENT_HANDOFF.md` after every material task.

Update `PROJECT_STATE.md` when project state, phase, blockers, environment status, or next step changes.

Run available verification commands before claiming completion. Use whatever exists in the repo, such as:

- lint;
- typecheck;
- build;
- unit tests;
- migration check;
- manual verification checklist.

If no automated checks exist yet, perform and report manual verification.

Final reports must include:

- branch;
- files changed;
- what was implemented;
- decisions made;
- tests/checks run;
- test results;
- blockers;
- deviations from instructions;
- next recommended step.

Do not say work is complete unless verification has been run or the absence of verification is explicitly reported.
